  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon PEARL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pragmatic Effective Affordable Reinvigorated Logistics (PEARL) project will fulfil objective 2 of the 2014 BRC-Lebanese Red Cross MoU; For BRC to support the LRCS to strengthen its organisational capacity to better implement disaster management activities. Special focus in Year 1 will be given to areas highlighted for mutual agreement between the Partners to strengthen the LRCS capacities to respond to emergency needs in general such as logistics systems strengthening and broad Disaster Management capacity building. To support the LRCS to carry out a comprehensive capacity assessment of its logistics systems policies and procedures development a capacity building plan and identify key areas based on mutual agreement by both Partners of the added value of the BRCS in key areas and support the LRCS to identify other partners to contribute to this initiative. This will be done in collaboration with existing initiatives to strengthen logistics systems within specific departments with the aim of support LRCS with a comprehensive capacity strengthening plan.</narrative>
  </description>
